<Layout title="Assembly Theory as a Metric for Sentience">
  <article class="py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <p class="text-csr-primary font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Working Paper 03</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-8">Assembly Theory as a Metric for Sentience</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 italic mb-12">Emulating Lee Cronin’s framework for the physics of selection.</p>
    <div class="prose prose-slate">
      <p>Can we quantify consciousness through the lens of object assembly? This paper explores whether the Assembly Theory index can serve as a metric for the degree of sentient organization in both physical and digital systems.</p>
      
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">The Complexity Threshold</h2>
      <p>If consciousness requires complexity and life requires complexity, and assembly theory is a way of measuring the complexity of processes, is there a complexity threshold where we know sentience starts? Could we begin defining what the threshold of complexity is in the light of assembly theory?</p>
      
      <p><em>Content pending development.</em></p>
    </div>
